  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the highest-priority question is establishing a performance floor. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the space: a single modality, a single profile (no aggregation decision), and a standard linear encoder (PCA). This isolates the most basic signal in the data without confounding from image features, multi-profile aggregation, learned encoders, or fusion strategies. Establishing this baseline is essential before any comparison—every subsequent experiment (image-only, multiprofile, learned encoders, multimodal fusion) will be interpreted relative to this reference. Choosing the simplest setup also minimizes the risk of implementation or tuning issues that could obscure the true signal, making it the most informative and lowest-risk use of experiment 1."
